    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d582">

                <pb facs="0712" n="610" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg610"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/914: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-28T10:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 28, 1919,
                                10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.40
                            a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Chinese Government requests early information as to whether American Government
                    will advance $1,000,000 Chinese share Siberian Railway loan. I am informed
                    Japanese Minister called at Foreign Office stating his Government would be very
                    glad to furnish this money. Chinese Government hopes American Government will
                        <pb facs="0713" n="611" xml:id="pg611"/> make the advance as it desires to
                    maintain its independence in matter relating to the Siberian and Chinese Eastern
                    Railway[s]. I beg to request an early and favorable reply.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
